# PY-1: 1.37.1 vs master on py-asgi-stream.
# A = 1.37.1 (9c034c47), B = master ed75ffa14, which has 0daef33c
# "http: compress application responses of unknown length".
# One app process; counts only, on a 2-CPU box with a PMU.
JOB=py1-asgi-stream
REV_A=9c034c47765fc448ba0ae3787285b48644b65e4d
REV_B=ed75ffa14f2a2fe5281fbe0eb132f88e50a117a2
WORKLOAD=py-asgi-stream
CONNS=1 32
WARM=2
DUR=8
REPS=2
APP_PROCS=1
PERF=1
STRACE=1
PRIMARY=r_instructions
EXPECT=B (master) has higher r_instructions than A (1.37.1): the unknown-length response takes the compression check that 0daef33c added in nxt_http_compression.c; direction up, exact syscalls level. Not a claim at REPS=2: the recorded run gave +0.37 percent at c1 (null band 0.40) and +0.12 percent at c32 (null band 1.15); a claim needs more blocks
FALSIFY=null band over 5 percent; or r_instructions level or down at every cell; or rsys_*/asys_* counts that differ between A and B (then the change is not the compression check alone)
